# Sello Design Language

The **Product domain** (Dashboard, Product List, Add/Edit, Details, photos, filters, cards, forms, tables, toasts, Settings Phase 1) plus prior conversation refinements is the **official design language**. Treat it as the default for every future screen unless the user explicitly overrides it.

## Philosophy

Sello is a **Business Operating System**, not an admin panel or POS.

Calm · premium · approachable · minimal · intelligent · spacious · refined.

One cohesive product — never invent a parallel visual system. Prefer extending existing shared widgets (`lib/shared/widgets/`, theme tokens) over new one-off patterns. Do not regress to generic Material defaults.

## Visual

Soft surfaces, subtle canvas gradients, generous whitespace, rounded cards (`AppRadius`), soft shadows (`AppShadows`), light borders (`outlinePanel`), calm purple accents, limited color. Avoid visual noise, harsh shadows, heavy outlines, decorative clutter.

## Hierarchy

1. **Inform** → 2. **Guide** → 3. **Allow action**.  
Ask: *What decision is the business owner making?* Every block should inform, help decide, or complete an action.

Typography: closed roles per surface (title / subtitle / section+divider / label / value) — spacing and dividers carry hierarchy more than many font sizes. Product Details is the model.

## Components (reuse first)

| Pattern | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| Cards | Generous padding, consistent radius/elevation/spacing |
| Buttons | Shared heights/radii; primary obvious, secondary quiet |
| Forms | Logical groups, labels above; required fields get a pinkish soft-red `*` after the label (`SelloFieldLabel` / `required: true` on `SelloTextField`, `SelloDropdown`, `SettingsCompactField`); optional fields have no marker, tooltip, or “Optional” copy. `SelloInfoHint` is only for real explanations. Keep validation/errors visible; preserve draft data |
| Tables | Clean rows, generous spacing, minimal borders, clear alignment |
| Dialogs | Guided workflow, balanced layout, clear primary; detail vs edit patterns from Products |
| Dropdowns | Desktop: anchored popup (never cover field). Mobile: bottom sheet |
| Toasts | Desktop top-right content-sized; mobile bottom safe-area. Use `SelloSnackbars` / `SelloToastHost` |
| Empty/loading | `SelloEmptyState`, skeletons / progressive load — avoid blocking overlays |
| Media | Immediate preview; optimize/upload in background |

## Interaction

Reduce friction. Prefer background work + progressive updates + instant feedback (filters, toasts). Archive over hard delete; confirm destructive actions. Match existing motion (`AppDurations` / `AppCurves`).

## Before shipping a screen

Check spacing, type, cards, interactions, color, motion, loading, empty states, responsiveness, and a11y against Products/Dashboard. Proactively suggest refinements that improve consistency without inventing new languages.
